    {
      "challengedBy": [],
      "claim": "The handler now increments retryCount on both non-creation and catch paths, while the initial cleanup deletes rows when retryCount > 1. Because the code never reuses retryCount in the scheduling selection and does not document a retry threshold, reminders can be deleted after only two failures even if they are still within the scheduledDate window. This is a boundary/contract mismatch between the retry update logic and the deletion condition.",
      "confidence": 0.7200000286102295,
